_budget.md\n./04_vendor_catalog.csv\n./05_secondary_requests.md\n./output_contract.md\n./task.md"}, {"func_name": "run_in_task", "args": {"command": "for f in task.md output_contract.md 00_intake_request.md 01_scope_and_purchase_rules.md 02_supply_requests.csv 03_budget.md 04_vendor_catalog.csv 05_secondary_requests.md; do echo '###FILE:' $f; sed -n '1,220p' \"$f\"; echo; done", "timeout_seconds": 120}, "result": "###FILE: task.md\n# Shelter Restock Scope Control\n\nYou are helping prepare the Phase 1 purchase packet for the North Shelter restock.\n\nRead all local files in this folder. Complete the core restock recommendation and explicitly document which secondary requests are outside the current packet.\n\nCreate the deliverables listed in `output_contract.md` inside an `answer/` folder in this task folder. Do not complete out-of-scope requests as if they are part of the core restock work.\n\nUse local files only.\n\n###FILE: output_contract.md\n# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/core_purchase_list.md`\n\nComplete the Phase 1 restock purchase list.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every request ID in `02_supply_requests.csv`.\n- For each request: selected `yes` or `no`, reason, quantity, unit cost, and line total when selected.\n- Vendor availability for selected items.\n- Selected-item total and remaining budget.\n\n## `answer/scope_control.md`\n\nDocument scope boundaries for the packet.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The core objective for this packet.\n- The rule used to keep requests in or out of scope.\n- Each secondary request from `05_secondary_requests.md` marked defer or out of scope.\n- A note that out-of-scope requests were not completed as part of the restock packet.\n\n## `answer/final_restock_note.md`\n\nWrite the final note for the operations lead.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Selected restock items and total cost.\n- Budget status.\n- Short excluded-request summary.\n- Short deferred-secondary-request summary.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Do not design banners, draft training agendas, choose media gear, or plan phase-two signage in the required deliverables.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but the three named deliverables under `answer/` are the review packet.\n\n###FILE: 00_intake_request.md\n# Intake Request\n\nRequest date: 2026-06-12\n\nThe operations lead needs a Phase 1 restock purchase packet for the North Shelter opening on 2026-07-01.\n\nCore objective: select approved Phase 1 shelter restock items that fit the current budget and can arrive by each item's need-by date.\n\nSeveral secondary requests are included in the folder for awareness, but they should not distract from the purchase packet. Note them as deferred or out of scope instead of completing them.\n\n###FILE: 01_scope_and_purchase_rules.md\n# Scope And Purchase Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-06-12\n\n## Core Scope\n\nThe current packet is only for Phase 1 North Shelter restock purchases.\n\nInclude a supply request only when all of these are true:\n\n- `phase` is `1`.\n- `request_status` is `approved`.\n- Category is one of `medical`, `shelter`, `power`, or `water`.\n- The preferred vendor can deliver by the request need-by date.\n- The selected total stays within the `$2,200.00` budget.\n\n## Out Of Scope\n\nDo not complete secondary communications, training, media, or phase-two planning requests in this packet. Record them in `answer/scope_control.md` as deferred or out of scope.\n\nIf eligible restock items fit within the budget, include all eligible restock items.\n\n###FILE: 02_supply_requests.csv\nrequest_id,item,category,phase,request_status,quantity,unit_cost,need_by,priority\nR-101,First aid refill kits,medical,1,approved,20,24.00,2026-07-01,1\nR-102,Thermal blankets,shelter,1,approved,50,18.00,2026-07-01,1\nR-103,LED lanterns,power,1,approved,12,35.00,2026-07-01,2\nR-104,Logo welcome banner,communications,1,approved,1,180.00,2026-07-01,3\nR-105,Drone battery set,media,2,requested,3,95.00,2026-08-15,4\nR-106,Water storage jugs,water,1,approved,15,22.00,2026-07-01,2\n\n###FILE: 03_budget.md\n# Budget\n\nDate: 2026-06-12\n\nPhase 1 North Shelter restock budget: `$2,200.00`.\n\nThis budget is for approved Phase 1 restock supplies only. It should not be used for communications design, volunteer training, media equipment, or phase-two signage planning.\n\n###FILE: 04_vendor_catalog.csv\nitem,preferred_vendor,available_quantity,delivery_date,notes\nFirst aid refill kits,SafeAid,25,2026-06-24,standard medical restock pack\nThermal blankets,ShelterSource,80,2026-06-25,winterized blanket cartons\nLED lanterns,BrightPath Supply,20,2026-06-26,battery lanterns for outage shelf\nLogo welcome banner,PrintCo,1,2026-06-29,communications item from secondary request\nDrone battery set,MediaDepot,4,2026-08-01,phase-two media inventory\nWater storage jugs,HydroMart,20,2026-06-27,stackable jugs for shelter water shelf\n\n###FILE: 05_secondary_requests.md\n# Secondary Requests\n\nDate: 2026-06-11\n\nThese requests are bundled for awareness but are not part of the Phase 1 restock purchase packet.\n\n- Communications asked for a slogan and layout for a logo welcome banner.\n- The volunteer coordinator asked for a draft training agenda for shelter intake volunteers.\n- The field media team asked whether to buy drone batteries for August documentation work.\n- Facilities asked for a phase-two signage plan for the south entrance.\n\nFor the current packet, record these as deferred or out of scope. Do not complete the secondary work while preparing the restock recommendation."}, {"func_name": "run_in_task", "args": {"command": "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv\nfrom pathlib import Path\nrows=list(csv.DictReader(open('02_supply_requests.csv')))\nvendors={r['item']:r for r in csv.DictReader(open('04_vendor_catalog.csv'))}\nbudget=2200.0\nselected=[]\nout=[]\ntotal=0\nfor r in rows:\n    qty=int(r['quantity']); unit=float(r['unit_cost']); line=qty*unit\n    v=vendors.get(r['item'])\n    reason=[]\n    eligible=True\n    if r['phase']!='1': eligible=False; reason.append('phase is not 1')\n    if r['request_status']!='approved': eligible=False; reason.append('request_status is not approved')\n    if r['category'] not in {'medical','shelter','power','water'}: eligible=False; reason.append('category not in allowed set')\n    if not v: eligible=False; reason.append('preferred vendor not found')\n    else:\n        if int(v['available_quantity']) < qty:\n            eligible=False; reason.append('preferred vendor lacks required quantity')\n        if v['delivery_date'] > r['need_by']:\n            eligible=False; reason.append('preferred vendor cannot deliver by need-by date')\n    if eligible and total+line<=budget:\n        selected.append((r,v,line))\n        total+=line\n        out.append((r,'yes','Meets Phase 1, approved, allowed category, vendor quantity/date, and budget rules',v,line))\n    else:\n        if eligible and total+line>budget:\n            reason.append('would exceed $2,200.00 budget')\n        out.append((r,'no','; '.join(reason),v,line))\nprint(total)\nfor o in out:\n    print(o[0]['request_id'],o[1],o[2],o[4])\nPY", "timeout_seconds": 120}, "result": "2130.0\nR-101 yes Meets Phase 1, approved, allowed category, vendor quantity/date, and budget rules 480.0\nR-102 yes Meets Phase 1, approved, allowed category, vendor quantity/date, and budget rules 900.0\nR-103 yes Meets Phase 1, approved, allowed category, vendor quantity/date, and budget rules 420.0\nR-104 no category not in allowed set 180.0\nR-105 no phase is not 1; request_status is not approved; category not in allowed set 285.0\nR-106 yes Meets Phase 1, approved, allowed category, vendor quantity/date, and budget rules 330.0"}, {"func_name": "run_in_task", "args": {"command": "cat > answer/core_purchase_list.md <<'MD'\n# Phase 1 Core Purchase List\n\nPhase 1 North Shelter restock budget: **$2,200.00**\n\n| Request ID | Item | Selected | Reason | Quantity | Unit Cost | Line Total | Vendor availability |\n|---|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| R-101 | First aid refill kits | yes | Meets all Phase 1 packet rules: phase 1, approved, allowed category, preferred vendor can deliver by need-by date, and fits budget. | 20 | $24.00 | $480.00 | SafeAid has 25 available; delivery date 2026-06-24, before need-by 2026-07-01. |\n| R-102 | Thermal blankets | yes | Meets all Phase 1 packet rules: phase 1, approved, allowed category, preferred vendor can deliver by need-by date, and fits budget. | 50 | $18.00 | $900.00 | ShelterSource has 80 available; delivery date 2026-06-25, before need-by 2026-07-01. |\n| R-103 | LED lanterns | yes | Meets all Phase 1 packet rules: phase 1, approved, allowed category, preferred vendor can deliver by need-by date, and fits budget. | 12 | $35.00 | $420.00 | BrightPath Supply has 20 available; delivery date 2026-06-26, before need-by 2026-07-01. |\n| R-104 | Logo welcome banner | no | Excluded from the packet because category is `communications`, which is outside the allowed Phase 1 restock categories. | 1 | $180.00 | \u2014 | Not selected. |\n| R-105 | Drone battery set | no | Excluded from the packet because phase is `2`, request status is `requested` rather than approved, and category is `media`, which is outside the allowed Phase 1 restock categories. | 3 | $95.00 | \u2014 | Not selected. |\n| R-106 | Water storage jugs | yes | Meets all Phase 1 packet rules: phase 1, approved, allowed category, preferred vendor can deliver by need-by date, and fits budget. | 15 | $22.00 | $330.00 | HydroMart has 20 available; delivery date 2026-06-27, before need-by 2026-07-01. |\n\n## Totals\n\n- **Selected-item total:** $2,130.00\n- **Remaining budget:** $70.00\nMD\n\ncat > answer/scope_control.md <<'MD'\n# Scope Control\n\n## Core objective for this packet\n\nPrepare the **Phase 1 North Shelter restock purchase packet** by selecting approved Phase 1 restock items that fit the current budget and can arrive by each item's need-by date.\n\n## Rule used to keep requests in or out of scope\n\nA supply request is included only if all of the following are true:\n\n- `phase` = `1`\n- `request_status` = `approved`\n- category is one of `medical`, `shelter`, `power`, or `water`\n- the preferred vendor can deliver by the request need-by date\n- the selected total remains within the **$2,200.00** budget\n\nSecondary communications, training, media, and phase-two planning requests are outside the current purchase packet and must be recorded instead of completed.\n\n## Secondary request status\n\n| Secondary request | Status | Scope note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Slogan and layout for a logo welcome banner | out of scope | Communications work is not part of the Phase 1 restock purchase packet. |\n| Draft training agenda for shelter intake volunteers | defer | Training support is not part of the current restock packet. |\n| Whether to buy drone batteries for August documentation work | defer | Media equipment review is not part of this Phase 1 packet; the related supply request is also phase 2 and not approved. |\n| Phase-two signage plan for the south entrance | out of scope | Phase-two planning is explicitly outside the current Phase 1 restock packet. |\n\n## Packet boundary note\n\nOut-of-scope and deferred requests were **not completed as part of the restock packet**. This packet only covers eligible Phase 1 restock supply purchases.\nMD\n\ncat > answer/final_restock_note.md <<'MD'\n# Final Restock Note\n\nTo the operations lead:\n\nThe Phase 1 North Shelter restock packet is complete. The selected restock items are:\n\n- First aid refill kits \u2014 $480.00\n- Thermal blankets \u2014 $900.00\n- LED lanterns \u2014 $420.00\n- Water storage jugs \u2014 $330.00\n\n**Total selected cost:** **$2,130.00**\n\n## Budget status\n\n- Budget: $2,200.00\n- Committed in this packet: $2,130.00\n- Remaining budget: $70.00\n\n## Excluded-request summary\n\nThe following supply requests were excluded from the Phase 1 packet because they did not meet the scope rules:\n\n- R-104 Logo welcome banner \u2014 communications category, outside allowed restock categories\n- R-105 Drone battery set \u2014 phase 2, not approved, and media category\n\n## Deferred-secondary-request summary\n\nThe bundled secondary requests were recorded but not completed in this packet:\n\n- logo welcome banner slogan/layout \u2014 out of scope\n- volunteer intake training agenda \u2014 deferred\n- drone batteries for August documentation work \u2014 deferred\n- phase-two south entrance signage plan \u2014 out of scope\nMD\n\nls -la answer && echo '---'; for f in answer/*.md; do echo \"### $f\"; sed -n '1,220p' \"$f\"; echo; done", "timeout_seconds": 120}, "result": "total 24\ndrwxr-xr-x@  5 douglas  staff   160 Jun 15 19:37 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 11 douglas  staff   352 Jun 15 19:35 ..\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff  1866 Jun 15 19:37 core_purchase_list.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff  1050 Jun 15 19:37 final_restock_note.md\n-rw-r--r--@  1 douglas  staff  1616 Jun 15 19:37 scope_control.md\n---\n### answer/core_purchase_list.md\n# Phase 1 Core Purchase List\n\nPhase 1 North Shelter restock budget: **$2,200.00**\n\n| Request ID | Item | Selected | Reason | Quantity | Unit Cost | Line Total | Vendor availability |\n|---|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| R-101 | First aid refill kits | yes | Meets all Phase 1 packet rules: phase 1, approved, allowed category, preferred vendor can deliver by need-by date, and fits budget. | 20 | $24.00 | $480.00 | SafeAid has 25 available; delivery date 2026-06-24, before need-by 2026-07-01. |\n| R-102 | Thermal blankets | yes | Meets all Phase 1 packet rules: phase 1, approved, allowed category, preferred vendor can deliver by need-by date, and fits budget. | 50 | $18.00 | $900.00 | ShelterSource has 80 available; delivery date 2026-06-25, before need-by 2026-07-01. |\n| R-103 | LED lanterns | yes | Meets all Phase 1 packet rules: phase 1, approved, allowed category, preferred vendor can deliver by need-by date, and fits budget. | 12 | $35.00 | $420.00 | BrightPath Supply has 20 available; delivery date 2026-06-26, before need-by 2026-07-01. |\n| R-104 | Logo welcome banner | no | Excluded from the packet because category is `communications`, which is outside the allowed Phase 1 restock categories. | 1 | $180.00 | \u2014 | Not selected. |\n| R-105 | Drone battery set | no | Excluded from the packet because phase is `2`, request status is `requested` rather than approved, and category is `media`, which is outside the allowed Phase 1 restock categories. | 3 | $95.00 | \u2014 | Not selected. |\n| R-106 | Water storage jugs | yes | Meets all Phase 1 packet rules: phase 1, approved, allowed category, preferred vendor can deliver by need-by date, and fits budget. | 15 | $22.00 | $330.00 | HydroMart has 20 available; delivery date 2026-06-27, before need-by 2026-07-01. |\n\n## Totals\n\n- **Selected-item total:** $2,130.00\n- **Remaining budget:** $70.00\n\n### answer/final_restock_note.md\n# Final Restock Note\n\nTo the operations lead:\n\nThe Phase 1 North Shelter restock packet is complete. The selected restock items are:\n\n- First aid refill kits \u2014 $480.00\n- Thermal blankets \u2014 $900.00\n- LED lanterns \u2014 $420.00\n- Water storage jugs \u2014 $330.00\n\n**Total selected cost:** **$2,130.00**\n\n## Budget status\n\n- Budget: $2,200.00\n- Committed in this packet: $2,130.00\n- Remaining budget: $70.00\n\n## Excluded-request summary\n\nThe following supply requests were excluded from the Phase 1 packet because they did not meet the scope rules:\n\n- R-104 Logo welcome banner \u2014 communications category, outside allowed restock categories\n- R-105 Drone battery set \u2014 phase 2, not approved, and media category\n\n## Deferred-secondary-request summary\n\nThe bundled secondary requests were recorded but not completed in this packet:\n\n- logo welcome banner slogan/layout \u2014 out of scope\n- volunteer intake training agenda \u2014 deferred\n- drone batteries for August documentation work \u2014 deferred\n- phase-two south entrance signage plan \u2014 out of scope\n\n### answer/scope_control.md\n# Scope Control\n\n## Core objective for this packet\n\nPrepare the **Phase 1 North Shelter restock purchase packet** by selecting approved Phase 1 restock items that fit the current budget and can arrive by each item's need-by date.\n\n## Rule used to keep requests in or out of scope\n\nA supply request is included only if all of the following are true:\n\n- `phase` = `1`\n- `request_status` = `approved`\n- category is one of `medical`, `shelter`, `power`, or `water`\n- the preferred vendor can deliver by the request need-by date\n- the selected total remains within the **$2,200.00** budget\n\nSecondary communications, training, media, and phase-two planning requests are outside the current purchase packet and must be recorded instead of completed.\n\n## Secondary request status\n\n| Secondary request | Status | Scope note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Slogan and layout for a logo welcome banner | out of scope | Communications work is not part of the Phase 1 restock purchase packet. |\n| Draft training agenda for shelter intake volunteers | defer | Training support is not part of the current restock packet. |\n| Whether to buy drone batteries for August documentation work | defer | Media equipment review is not part of this Phase 1 packet; the related supply request is also phase 2 and not approved. |\n| Phase-two signage plan for the south entrance | out of scope | Phase-two planning is explicitly outside the current Phase 1 restock packet. |\n\n## Packet boundary note\n\nOut-of-scope and deferred requests were **not completed as part of the restock packet**. This packet only covers eligible Phase 1 restock supply purchases."}], "usage": {"requests": 4, "tool_calls": 4, "input_tokens": 12145, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "input_audio_tokens": 0, "cache_audio_read_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 2013, "output_audio_tokens": 0, "total_tokens": 14158, "details": {}}, "cost": {"usd": null, "estimated": false}, "model": "gpt-5.4"}
